# SAEA-BENCH-decode-q4km — decode-rate ATTRIBUTION probe (owner directive
# 2026-08-11: "decode 探针跑完把归因结果给我"). The observed decode is 10-20x
# below what a 3B-active MoE on this card should give (6.31 tok/s per slot at
# ~1.0k context, 3-4 at ~4.7k, vs a 60-150 tok/s realistic band), and THAT —
# not token accounting — is what makes large campaigns take days. Three
# single-delta configurations against the locked config A reference
# (fd7ba3: 6.31 tok/s per slot at 4-way), identical bare-core arm, same fast
# split, wall clock NOT the readout — per-slot decode rates from the server
# log are:
#
#   --model decode-c16k    -c 16384 (4k/slot)   M1: VRAM-spill hypothesis —
#                          if decode jumps when ~2.5 GB of KV reservation is
#                          returned, the 95.7%-full card is silently backing
#                          allocations with host memory (-ngl 999 disables
#                          llama.cpp's own fitting);
#   --model decode-f16kv   -ctk/-ctv f16 -c 24576   M2: quantized-KV
#                          flash-attention kernel path on sm_120 — f16 KV in
#                          VRAM isolates the kernel from the memory question
#                          (the 2026-08-09 f16 datum had KV in system RAM);
#   --model decode-np2     -np 2 -c 24576   M3: MoE batch-dimension
#                          efficiency — if per-slot rate nearly doubles at
#                          np2, 4-way batching buys little aggregate and the
#                          bottleneck is the batched MoE kernel itself.
#
# M3 (llama.cpp version upgrade) and the WSL dxgkrnl overhead are NOT probed
# here; the attribution from these three points decides whether the upgrade
# bench is the next move. vLLM is ruled out by owner judgment (2026-08-11).
#
# run_id:baseline_fragment
SAEA-BENCH-decode-q4km:bare-core-ojw
